      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“baḤodesh haRevi’i” (In the fourth month) attributed to Solomon ibn Gabirol is one of the seliḥot offered in the nusaḥ Sefaradi for the 17th of Tamuz. It can be found as transcribed here with an English translation in <tei:hi rend="italic">Siddur Siftei Tsadiqim (The Form of Prayers) vol. 6: Seder haTefilot laTaaniyot</tei:hi> (ed. Isaac Leeser 1838) p.107-109. I have made some minor adjustments, replacing ‘tables’ with ‘stela,’ re-Hebraizing divine names, and removing archaisms. –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_37858_notes"/>
